## 3. API Design

```
POST /v1/notifications/send            # transactional, single-user, near-real-time
  { user_id, template_id, params, priority }

POST /v1/campaigns                     # segment/broadcast campaign creation
  { template_id, segment_query, scheduled_at, delivery_window_minutes }

GET  /v1/campaigns/{id}/status         # delivery funnel: sent/delivered/opened counts

POST /v1/devices/register              # device registers/updates push token
  { user_id, device_id, platform, push_token, locale, timezone }

POST /v1/preferences                   # user updates category opt-in/out, quiet hours
  { user_id, category_flags, quiet_hours_start, quiet_hours_end }

POST /v1/webhooks/delivery-receipt     # provider callback: delivered / opened / token-invalid
```

Internal producers (content-catalog, recs engine, billing, live-event scheduler) call the transactional or campaign endpoints — they never talk to APNs/FCM directly.

