## 4. Data Model / Schema

### 4.1 Device Registry (Cassandra / DynamoDB — partition key: `device_id`)
```
Device
  device_id        PK
  user_id          indexed (secondary index or GSI)
  platform         ios | android | web | tv
  push_token       opaque string, rotates periodically
  app_version
  locale, timezone
  status           active | expired | invalid
  last_active_at
  created_at, updated_at
```
- **Write pattern**: high — token refreshes, app opens.
- **Read pattern**: point read by device_id (transactional dispatch) and by user_id (fan-out to all of a user's devices).
- **Token invalidation**: when a provider returns "token no longer valid" on a delivery attempt, the dispatcher writes back `status=invalid` — this table is the source of truth that keeps the segment index (below) clean.

### 4.2 User Preferences (partition key: `user_id`)
```
UserPreferences
  user_id                PK
  category_flags         map<text, bool>   e.g. {new_release: true, recs: false, downloads: true, marketing: false}
  quiet_hours_start       local time
  quiet_hours_end         local time
  timezone
  updated_at
```
- Single-partition point read — this is what backs the **transactional path** directly, with a Redis write-through cache for hot users (active in last 24h) to shave point-read latency further.

### 4.3 Segment Index (derived, NOT the canonical store — see Deep Dive 2)
```
SegmentIndex
  segment_key       PK   e.g. "new_release#US#bucket_0042"
  device_ids        set<text>, capped per bucket (~100K)
  updated_at
```
- Populated via CDC off `UserPreferences` + `Device` — never written to directly by application code.
- Bucketing exists specifically to avoid wide-partition problems at 10s of millions of members per raw segment key (see Deep Dive 2).

### 4.4 Notification Template & Campaign
```
NotificationTemplate
  template_id      PK
  type
  title, body, deep_link, image_ref
  ttl_seconds
  priority         high | normal

Campaign
  campaign_id      PK
  template_id      FK
  target_segment_query
  scheduled_at
  delivery_window_minutes
  status           draft | scheduled | canary | ramping | completed | failed
```

### 4.5 Delivery Log (append-only, time-partitioned — Cassandra/wide-column or a columnar store for analytics)
```
DeliveryLog
  notification_id   PK
  device_id, user_id, campaign_id
  status            queued | sent | delivered | failed | opened
  attempt_count
  provider_message_id
  error_code        (nullable)
  sent_at, delivered_at, opened_at
```
- Partitioned by `date + campaign_id` (or `date + shard`) to keep write hot-spots distributed and to make 30-day TTL cleanup a cheap partition-drop rather than row-by-row deletes.

