## How to Use This Bank

- Pick one question per mock session and time-box it to ~45 minutes, the way a real onsite round would run.
- Force yourself to state **capacity estimates** and a **rough data model** before drawing the high-level diagram — that ordering is itself part of the signal an interviewer is grading.
- After you land on an initial design, deliberately ask yourself the two hardest follow-ups from the probe list — most candidates get an adequate design; the differentiation at Staff level shows up in how you handle the probes, not the first draft.
- Categories **C (Platform Infrastructure)** and **A (Content Delivery)** are the most likely core rounds for a Netflix system design interview; **D (Account/Trust)** questions are a good stretch set if you want practice with less "textbook" prompts that don't map cleanly onto a known paper or blog post.
